eg;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"width:78px;\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\"><strong>Rishu</strong></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"width:90px;\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\">55&deg;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"width:72px;\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\">50&deg;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"width:78px;\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\">&nbsp;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"width:90px;\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\"><strong>360&deg;</strong></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"width:72px;\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"center\"><strong>360&deg;</strong></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p><br />\n<strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>As in the question, all the data is in degrees and we know that the total degree value is 360 which will be the same in both years. So we will solve this question in direct proportion without the use of a degree.</p>\n\n<p>Let the ratio of winning amount in the lucky draw of 2020 and 2021 be 5x and 19x. &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The amount of lucky draw won by Bupendero, Rajesh and Rishu together in 2020 = 75 + 60 + 55</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 190</p>\n\n<p>Total amount = 5x &times; 190</p>\n\n<p>The amount of lucky draw won by Sandeep Sucheta and Abhishek 2021 together in 2021:</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 70 + 75 + 65</p>\n\n<p>Total amount = 19x &times; 210</p>\n\n<p>Required ratio = (5x &times; 190) ∶&nbsp;(19x &times; 210)</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 5&nbsp;: 21</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The ratio of the total amount won by Bupendero, Rajesh and Rishu in 2020 together is to total amount won by Sandeep Sucheta and Abhishek 2021 together is 5&nbsp;</strong>∶<strong>&nbsp;21.</strong></p>",
