          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p align=\"left\">We know that sum of all the values (a and b) in each chart equal to 100.</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">So, we have</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">3a + 8a + 7a + 4a + 3a = 100 &rArr; 25a = 100 &rArr; a = 4</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Similarly, 2b + 6b + 5b + 4b + 3b = 100 &rArr; 20b = 100 &rArr; b = 5</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Now it&rsquo;s given in question that rice production in Kerala is 21 million metric tons</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Kerala produce 4b% of rice in India that is 20% rice</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">So. We have 20% of rice in India = 21 million metric tons</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Rice production in India = (21 &times; 100)/20 = 105 million metric tons</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Now rice production in India is 7a% &rArr; 28% of total rice production in world</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Therefore, rice production in world = (105 &times; 100)/28 = 375 million metric tons</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">The third highest rice production state in India is Kerala which produce 21 million metric tons of rice.</p>\n\n<p align=\"left\">Its contribution to world is (21/375) &times; 100 = 5.6%</p>",
